utely got destroyed  on the play he got pushed back  and what can he do look at the left  tackle watch the left tackle i want you  to watch the left tackle  what can josh do when your left tackle  is getting totally annihilated like that  what can he do so that's why i say i  really didn't have a a problem with the  actual call but these guys have to come  ready to play and deion dawkins did not  want it he did not want it and look at  him he's on his back he's a 300 pounder  it's the most critical play of the game  and he had a mental lapse and he got  physically handled so i didn't have a  problem with it but he has to do his job  i thought that happened a lot in this  game tennessee just played so hard up  front they got that verbal attitude  about them but i thought there was a lot  of moments where you just saw  tennessee's defensive front bullying the  offensive line of buffalo we haven't  really seen that happen much this year  but in one of the biggest moments of the  game like you just pointed out it looked  like tennessee was thinking quarterback  sneak quarterback sneak they reacted  just like that getting that initial push  which blew up to play i want to hear  from coach mcdermott on the decision to  go for it and the call that ensued here  was the head coach on a tough one that  resulted in a loss  far from from winning the game  and i owe that to my players and  you know i believe in my players i  believe in our quarterback um  so  i trust my guys  obviously we didn't get it done in this  case um but i trust my players  didn't work out in our favor obviously  didn't have the greatest footing  um  it happens  game of inches  you know the gate the the play before  was pretty close too um  didn't turn out in our favor today you  know felt  you know hey if we're that far from  potentially winning the game right there  was the best thing we could do we hadn't  stopped him on defense  for for  a number of drives there in the second  half really so  but agai